# Our own RTN W4A16 group-128 quant of Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (see
# tools/quant_flashnext.py) — same precision map and tensor format as the
# aixiaoma reference: routed experts int4/group-128, everything else BF16,
# PLE table BF16 in pinned host RAM. Produced by the overnight chain from
# the BF16 source at /srv/llm/Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next.
#
# EXPERIMENTAL bring-up profile (FLASHNEXT_PROFILE=qwen3.8-flash-next-w4rtng128).
# Known blockers before it can serve (see todo real-model-bringup):
#   1. PLE table is still allocated on GPU at init under offload
#      (~25.6 GiB/rank at TP4 + ~15.8 GiB main shard > 32 GiB GPU) — needs
#      the patch-v2 init-skip before load can succeed.
#   2. torch.compile hits an upstream 2a4cd640 ConstraintViolationError on
#      this model — run eager (mode 0) until a fixed ref is available.
VLLM_MODEL=/srv/llm/kurt/flashnext-w4a16-rtng128
VLLM_TOKENIZER=/srv/llm/kurt/flashnext-w4a16-rtng128
VLLM_SERVED_NAME=qwen3.8-flash-next-w4rtng128
VLLM_TP=4
VLLM_GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.60
VLLM_KV_CACHE_DTYPE=bfloat16
VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=196608
VLLM_MAX_BATCHED_TOKENS=16384
VLLM_MAX_NUM_SEQS=1
VLLM_PLE_CPU_OFFLOAD=1
# Unquoted + space-free JSON: compose strips quotes only at value start and
# the entrypoint word-splits VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS.
VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS=--enable-expert-parallel --compilation-config {"mode":0}
